#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143741} :activity/id #uuid "b5ec396d-4177-5616-8f79-caa14470e518" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048987 :topic/id #uuid "d12cbe5f-b948-5cf0-8d57-b3147ff8483b" :topic/math-academy-id 2437} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143741 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186144099 :tutorial/content "Remember that a *unit fraction* contains $\\color{blue}1$ in the numerator. \n\nFor example, the following fractions are unit fractions since they each contain ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}{2}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}{5}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}{8}\n$$\n\nHowever, the following fractions are *not-unit* fractions since they do *not* contain ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}{2}}{3}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{red}{5}}{8}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{red}{7}}{12}\n$$\n\nIn this lesson, we will use models to divide whole numbers by *non-unit* fractions. \n\n**Note**: Throughout this lesson, we'll be drawing numerous fraction models. It is highly recommended that you draw these models on a piece of paper to better understand their workings." :tutorial/id #uuid "808c4b1b-413d-5280-9a9b-06fe6c276e1e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9727 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0d7ac216-ae96-58b0-a9ce-2e8170fa53e3" :step/math-academy-id 195012 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143742}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143742 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186144100 :tutorial/content "Let's use a model to find the result of the following division problem:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div \\dfrac26\n$$\n\nWe start with a model that represents ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ whole:\n\n![](images/38/38a8f6963fbe538fc67310e583271d8feeef3b86ec9f1e81354f179fe727963f.png)\n\n \n\nWe need to determine how many times $\\dfrac26$ fits into ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ whole. So, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split our whole into *sixths* (the denominator of our fraction):\n\n![](images/e2/e2755b6a9d635d016f882865251e7614cfd510d667f7e3097f1b111e2fa8fceb.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups, where each group contains $\\dfrac26{:}$\n\n![](images/1f/1f5112d7cdc2b618184868432410e0cea855cce6523de7649bef3761994325bd.png)\n\n \n\n- Finally, we count the groups. We see that there are $\\color{purple} 3$ groups in total.\n\n![](images/cb/cb3f646178db5af92710e87620b3f3acf7b2a5f0b8ef40deffaa75db435622e6.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $\\color{blue}1$ whole into groups of ${\\color{black}{\\dfrac26}},$ we get ${\\color{purple}{3}}$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div {\\color{black}\\dfrac26} = {\\color{purple}3}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7a0e1f53-a27a-521f-ae26-acc6bf0a9cf7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9941 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "d108e3ea-1e1e-5525-a53f-5fa965cff768" :step/math-academy-id 195013 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143743}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143743 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142845 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142655 :question/id #uuid "7f3801c4-d25f-57e0-85b3-b52df08d7072" :question/math-academy-id "e-15654"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f7df9be-867f-56b1-85d3-00ad838dc054" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049439} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050665}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143530} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143544} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440722} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440725} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440727} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440729} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440733}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Number"} :step/id #uuid "e00f034a-54de-5628-a57d-18faffe995cc" :step/math-academy-id 195014 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143744}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143744 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142846 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142637 :question/id #uuid "be59814b-3823-57b9-9a2c-f678e1d34183" :question/math-academy-id "e-14203"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c692a59-11d5-5b7c-868c-438cfd23a04f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143254} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143255} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440721} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440723} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440724} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440732}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Missing Numbers"} :step/id #uuid "a926d207-1695-5aa3-9eb3-c4570678537b" :step/math-academy-id 195017 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143745}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143745 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142847 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142636 :question/id #uuid "23532ee6-f05b-5ac7-b722-84891afd3bc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14197"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5587f6-f6a7-523c-b532-15786ade73b7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143256} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186143257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440726} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440728} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440730} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440731}] :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Whole Number by a Non-Unit Fraction"} :step/id #uuid "f64e3d2e-90f6-5dc1-b01f-8fea17eee52b" :step/math-academy-id 195021}] :activity/title "Dividing Whole Numbers by Fractions Using Models: Whole Number Results" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186143063}]}
